@host = https://localhost:7202

### 1) Send the email OTP (in Development the code is logged to the console)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/registration/otp/send
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "john.doe@gmail.com"
}

### 1b) Resend the OTP (subject to the 60s cooldown + per-email cap)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/registration/otp/resend
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "john.doe@gmail.com"
}

### 2) Verify the OTP (use the code from the console log)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/registration/otp/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "john.doe@gmail.com",
  "code": "123456"
}

### 3) Create the account (email is the username; includes the registration screen's personal info)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/registration/account
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "John",
  "lastName": "Doe",
  "dateOfBirth": "1990-05-15",
  "zipCode": "12345",
  "email": "john.doe@gmail.com",
  "contactNumber": "123-456-7890",
  "password": "Str0ng!Pass",
  "confirmPassword": "Str0ng!Pass"
}

### Health
GET {{host}}/health
